# GOTCHA: Striven (and the Supabase Management API) sit behind Cloudflare —
# every request MUST send a browser User-Agent, else HTTP 403 "error 1010".

# ── Dashboard login (username + password) ────────────────────────────────────
# ONLY SOURCE = Supabase table `public.dashboard_users` (username, password),
# read live by the backend over PostgREST with the service-role key (RLS on, so
# only the server key can read it — anon is blocked). Passwords are stored
# scrypt-hashed; to change one, log in as that user with the new password only
# after replacing the row, or hash it with hashPassword() in api/_striven.js.
# Username match is case-insensitive, ".com" optional; passwords case-SENSITIVE.
# 2026-07-18 (HIPAA): the plaintext APP_USERS env fallback and the shared
# ACCESS_PASSWORD gate were REMOVED from code, from this file, from
# striven-server/.env and from Supabase app_config. No login credential exists
# outside the hashed table, and auth fails closed if the table is unreachable.
# 2026-07-20 (USER REQUEST): passwords set back to Firstname@2026 at the owner's
# explicit instruction, after flagging the HIPAA weakness (guessable format on a
# PHI-access dashboard). Still scrypt-hashed in the DB; stored live via PATCH.
# NOTE: these are weak/guessable — recommend rotating to strong values again.
# Current passwords — the only working copy now lives here (hashed in the DB):
APP_USER_1=rishi@sportsmedrecovery.com      / Rishi@2026
APP_USER_2=crystal@sportsmedrecovery.com    / Crystal@2026
APP_USER_3=admin@sportsmedrecovery.com      / Admin@2026   # owner/admin
# Supabase (project "Dashboard") tables:
#   dashboard_users(username,password)   — logins, scrypt-hashed
#   app_config(key,value)                — STRIVEN_* + QB_* creds (no passwords)
#   login_events(username,success,ip,at) — audit: who logged in, when
#   phi_access_events(username,path,ip,at)— audit: who read patient data (HIPAA)
# Supabase service-role key (server-side only; set as Vercel env SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY
# + in striven-server/.env). Powerful — bypasses RLS. Rotate if leaked.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY_NOTE="in striven-server/.env + Vercel env; reads dashboard_users"

# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
